> bounded sin(x)
bounded sin(x):
  bounded (on all real x)
  above: proved by interval arithmetic: f <= 1; the largest value seen is 1 at x = -4.71238898 (~-3*pi/2)
  below: proved by interval arithmetic: f >= -1; the smallest value seen is -1 at x = -7.853981634 (~-5*pi/2)
> bounded 1/(1 + x^2)
bounded 1/(x^2 + 1):
  bounded (on all real x)
  above: proved by interval arithmetic: f <= 1; the largest value seen is 1 at x = 0
  below: proved by interval arithmetic: f >= 0; the smallest value seen is 0.009900990099 at x = -10
> bounded x^2 - 4
bounded x^2 - 4:
  bounded below, not above (on all real x)
  above: proved: a polynomial of degree 2 with leading coefficient 1: f -> +inf as x -> +inf
  below: proved: an even-degree polynomial with a positive leading coefficient has a minimum, -4 at x = 0 (a root of f')
> bounded x^3
bounded x^3:
  unbounded above and below (on all real x)
  above: proved: a polynomial of degree 3 with leading coefficient 1: f -> +inf as x -> +inf
  below: proved: a polynomial of degree 3 with leading coefficient 1: f -> -inf as x -> -inf
> bounded exp(x)
bounded exp(x):
  bounded below, not above (on all real x)
  above: f(100) = 2.688117142e+43, beyond any value on [-10, 10] (checked numerically)
  below: proved by interval arithmetic: f >= 0; the smallest value seen is 4.539992976e-05 at x = -10
> bounded 1/x in 1..2
bounded 1/x:
  bounded on [1, 2]
  above: proved by interval arithmetic: f <= 1; the largest value seen is 1 at x = 1
  below: proved by interval arithmetic: f >= 0.5; the smallest value seen is 0.5 at x = 2
